[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 703,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 466,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105969,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 165,
        "headingId": 466,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Papillary intralymphatic angioendothelioma (PILA) and retiform haemangioendothelioma (RHE) are locally aggressive, rarely metastasizing lymphatic tumours with hobnail endothelia, which may represent a spectrum rather than different types.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:46:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 704,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 467,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105970,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 165,
        "headingId": 467,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9135/1 Papillary intralymphatic angioendothelioma</p>\r\n<p>9136/1 Retiform haemangioendothelioma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:46:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 705,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 468,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105971,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 165,
        "headingId": 468,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2B56.1 &amp; XH4SY7 Angiosarcoma of skin &amp; Papillary intralymphatic angioendothelioma</p>\r\n<p>2B56.1 &amp; XH64U8 Angiosarcoma of skin &amp; Retiform haemangioendothelioma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:46:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 706,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 469,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105972,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 165,
        "headingId": 469,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> Dabska tumour; endovascular papillary angioendothelioma; hobnail haemangioendothelioma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:46:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 707,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 470,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105973,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 165,
        "headingId": 470,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:46:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 708,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 471,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105974,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 165,
        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>PILA and RHE usually affect the superficial soft tissue of the lower extremities {10478659}. Cases of PILA have been reported in the oral cavity, spleen, and bone {15061715; 18090926; 29423171}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:46:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105975,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 165,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>PILA and RHE manifest as slow-growing, cutaneous, pink-violaceous nodules or plaques. With both PILA and RHE, a concurrent lymphatic malformation (lymphangioma) or lymphoedema may be observed {21915027; 10478659; 27730656}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:46:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105976,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 165,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>With &lt;&nbsp;50&nbsp;cases of each reported, PILA occurs predominantly in children and young adults, whereas RHE occurs mainly in adolescents and young adults {21238627; 9274963; 25484427; 8291650; 8764941}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:46:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105977,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 165,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:46:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105978,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 165,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:46:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105979,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 165,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>PILA and RHE are poorly defined infiltrative tumours, usually involving the dermis and subcutis. Sizes range from 10&nbsp;to 400&nbsp;mm, with a mean of 70&nbsp;mm for PILA, which is often a more extensive lesion, whereas in most cases RHE is small and measures &lt;&nbsp;30&nbsp;mm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T13:46:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105980,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 165,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "<p>PILA is composed of columnar, matchstick-like endothelial cells. Papillary tufts of these hobnail endothelial cells surrounding hyaline cores protrude into the lumen of dilated lymphatic spaces; lymphatics may be slit-like with intraluminal glomeruloid endothelial proliferations. Proteinaceous fluid and intraluminal and stromal lymphocytes support the lymphatic phenotype and association. There should not be significant endothelial atypia or mitoses; such cases would instead be classified as angiosarcoma. RHE is also poorly circumscribed with hobnail cells and a lymphatic appearance that tends to have a densely sclerotic stroma and an arborizing pattern that resembles normal rete testis. RHE can be one component of composite haemangioendothelioma.</p>\r\n<p>Both PILA and RHE stain for lymphatic markers (PILA stains for podoplanin [recognized by D2-40], PROX1, VEGFR3, or VEGFR2; RHE stains for PROX1 and occasionally D2-40) as well as endothelial markers (CD31, CD34, and ERG). SMA should be positive around the larger lymphatic spaces and may be absent within the papillary tufting {32031140; 22067331; 10478659; 19674202; 24282657}. The presence of SMA also separates these entities from angiosarcoma.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-20T13:44:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
